CompatibilityRemote

# User-requested design refresh for Experimental Yeet Remote (web) only.
# The native ContentView remains reserved for the user's OpenPencil design.

Shell: fixed app frame; the document never scrolls, only panes do
  Layers, low to high (named z tokens, no ad-hoc values): canvas and Main, floating bars, scrim, panes, sheet, toast
    Canvas: the app background; Main is flat on it, with no frame or border of its own
    Panes: LeftNavigation and WorkspacePanel are inset 8px from the window, 16px corners, a hairline ring plus soft shadow instead of borders
      Wide: stay in the layout so no content is covered; narrow: the same surface overlays Main above a scrim
    Corners: 6px inline (code, chips), 8px controls and rows inside a pane (16px surface minus 8px inset), 16px surfaces (panes, composer, sheets, bubbles)
    Blur: ProgressiveBlur is the only blur material and marks "above what scrolls beneath": under the title bar and above the composer on the conversation, behind drawers (edge) and sheets (uniform)
      Blur layers are siblings of animated views, never descendants (an ancestor's opacity hides the backdrop); prefers-reduced-transparency turns blur off for solid bars
  LeftNavigation: 264px source list, collapsible; overlay below 900px
    Header: 44px, on the title-bar line; Yeet mark, close navigation
    NewSession: full-width row action
    ScrollRegion: independently scrollable, min-height 0
      Navigation: Sessions, Files, Diff, Agents, Scheduled tasks, Debate; icon + label + optional count
        Rows: 30px pointer, 44px touch; selection is fill plus weight
      SessionSearch
      RecentSessions: title, relative age, selected and running state
    Footer: connection state only while not connected, Settings; always reachable
  Main: flexible, min-width 0
    TitleBar: 44px; floats over the transcript on a top blur on the conversation, solid with a rule on other pages; navigation toggle, page title + one line of context, page controls, run state, connection problem, workspace-panel toggle
      Context: current folder (Files), change totals (Review changes); never a second page header
      PageControls: segmented choice owned by the page (Review changes: Changes / Full file)
      RunState: spinner + elapsed when a session works and the page is not the conversation; opens it
      Connection: text only when not connected
    StatusBar: 28px, wide pointer layouts only; workspace path, branch, changed-files action
      No nominal states (connected, idle, no changes); hidden below 900px and on touch
    Conversation: independently scrollable, centered readable column (~760px); runs the full height of Main, padded so its first and last lines clear the floating bars
      Messages: generous rhythm, quiet tool disclosures, keyboard-visible actions
      ToolLists: Codex-style compact steps; flat, not a stack of cards
        Order: always-visible calls from top to bottom in backend order; no aggregate header/title or step count
        Row: aligned tool icon, action and distinct context, individual disclosure chevron
        Context: single-line preview; full value available in expanded details
        CallList: equal left alignment for all calls; consistent 4px gaps and 8px row padding
        Details: quiet inset rail beneath its own call; no extra group nesting
        ExpandedStep: labeled arguments/output, selectable literal text, bounded scroll region
          Shell: working directory, literal command with prompt, separate stdout/stderr, exit state
            Live jobs: existing shell viewer; no command is launched by expanding a record
          Edit: per-file unified diff, old/new line numbers, +/− and green/red rows, warnings
          Read: per-file source with line numbers and captured range; explicit preview/missing states
          Diagnostics: severity, file location, message; never hidden in raw JSON
          Search: query/scope and individually readable source or web matches
          OtherTools: labeled human-readable fields/text; never raw JSON by default
          RawInspection: secondary disclosure for original input/output; backend owns expansion
          PartialData: truncation, tail, background handoff, and artifact references remain explicit
        State: only active progress and consequential exceptions; no routine success badges
          Label, context and attention {approval | problem} come from the Rust trace projection
        Interaction: native buttons, Enter/Space, expanded state and controlled-region relationship
        Mobile: >=44px disclosure targets; exception text wraps without crowding context
      EmptyState: centered greeting and workspace context
      FollowOutput: pinned only while near bottom; floating Jump to latest when reading history
    Composer: floats over the bottom of the transcript on a bottom blur; its measured height pads the transcript and positions Jump to latest; same column alignment, one bordered flat surface, auto-growing field
      NewChatWorkspace: labeled native workspace choice beside input, only for an empty new chat
        Open another workspace path action; never a workspace selector in left sidebar
      Controls: one quiet row; attachment, model, reasoning, context, send/stop
        Phone: same single row; context does not take a line of its own
      Context: compact percentage plus accessible used/limit token information
      No explanatory helper copy beneath the composer
  WorkspacePanel: 320px, collapsible, visible by default at >=1280px
    Header: 44px, on the title-bar line; workspace name, refresh, close
    Context: one line for path and branch, one for change summary
    Tabs: segmented Status (default), Changes, Files; count for changes
    Status: flat rows without dividers; model, reasoning, context, usage, provider limits and reset windows
      Quiet defaults omitted: state only while working or disconnected; agents only when active
      Usage: input and output tokens always; reasoning, cache and model-call rows only when reported
      Cost: backend-reported estimate only for metered/API usage; hidden for subscriptions
      MissingData: explicit not reported; never invent cost from credits or token counts
    ScrollRegion: live backend-provided entries, selection and empty states
      Changes: file paths, additions/deletions, selected patch, full-page review action
      Files: directory navigation, selected file metadata, full-page browse action
    StatusNavigation: Manage providers & authentication; agents available in main navigation
    Overlay: below 1280px; scrim, Escape dismissal, focus containment and restoration
  Pages: content starts at the top of the pane; the title bar names the page
  DiffPage: narrow 180px file rail, flexible independently scrolling patch
    FileIdentity: workspace-relative paths, selection and +/- counts
    Compact: bounded file list above patch on narrow layouts
  FilesPage: 240px directory rail beside file preview/metadata, each independently scrolling
    Path: current directory in the title bar; Parent folder is the first list row; folder/file glyphs and separate change status
    Preview: bounded backend-provided numbered text; binary/large/error states explicit

Responsiveness
  Composer-only updates do not rebuild transcript; linear item spacing computation
  Coalesce editor synchronization while typing; submit carries exact latest text
  Shell-job output does not invalidate unrelated application views
  Navigation feedback is immediate; never fake completion to conceal network latency

VisualLanguage
  Standalone app, not a website: app chrome at 13px, reading column at 15px; chrome text is not selectable.
  Existing theme palette; distinct navigation and composer; subtle borders, flat supporting controls.
  Segmented control for few peer choices; selected segment raised and bold, aria-pressed.
  Icon toolbar buttons: 28px pointer, 44px touch, accessible name and tooltip.
  Light/dark via existing appearance setting; no new business logic or protocol.
  Consistent outline icons, 8px spacing rhythm, readable sentence-case section labels.
  Shared reading-column tokens align conversation, tool lists, and composer text.
  Sidebar: clear session grouping, quiet selection, labeled Settings footer.
  Inspector: flat tab strip and bounded patch preview; no unnecessary nested surfaces.
  Restrained panel entrances, hover/press/focus feedback; respect reduced motion.
  Touch targets >=44px; safe-area padding; no horizontal document overflow.
  Navigation and workspace drawers are mutually exclusive on narrow screens.
  Corners: three radii by role (inline 6, control 8, surface 12); no pills or glow rings.
  Activity: small hollow spinner ring with transparent center; respect reduced motion.
  Copy: omit explanatory subtitles and helper paragraphs; retain labels, live context, errors and consequential warnings.
